| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/store/kanban.js` | Modify | `actions.newSprintTask` | Destructure `getters` from the action context; compute `firstColumn = getters.sprintColumns?.[0]`; set `board = parentChat?.board \|\| sprintId` and `column = parentChat?.column \|\| firstColumn?.title \|\| taskStatus` **before** `createNewChat`, and pass `board`/`column` into the create payload and the defensive `updateChatInfo` updates alongside `sprints`/`status`. |

## 4. Why this is the right, minimal fix

- **Non-null before save:** `board` and `column` are now always part of the `createNewChat` payload, so the backend `PUT /api/chats?chat_only=1` receives them at creation time — no more "missing board/column" failure.
- **Correct target:** the new root task is pinned to the active sprint board (`state.activeBoard`) and its **first column** (`sprintColumns[0].title`, i.e. `"To Do"`).
- **Subtasks preserved:** when `parentId` is present, the parent's existing `board`/`column` still take precedence, keeping the parent→child linkage intact.
- **Sprint semantics untouched:** grouping still uses `status` and membership still uses `sprints`; `column` merely satisfies the required field and mirrors the first column name.
- **No contract changes:** callers (`SprintBoardModals`/`SprintBoardView`) and other actions (`newTask`, `createSubTask`, board flows) are unchanged.

> Note: if you prefer the sprint "column" to be stored as the status **value** (`"todo"`) rather than the column **title** (`"To Do"`), change `firstColumn?.title` to `firstColumn?.value`. The title form is recommended for consistency with how `column` is represented elsewhere (e.g. `createNewBoardChat({ columnTitle })`, `TaskSettings` binding to `column.title`).

